## REST endpoints

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| GET | /cases | list all cases |
| POST | /cases | create a case |
| GET | /cases/{id} | get a single case |
| PUT | /cases/{id} | update a case |
| POST | /cases/{id}/classify | trigger AI classification |
| POST | /cases/{id}/escalate | manually escalate |
| POST | /cases/{id}/resolve | resolve a case |
| GET | /cases/{id}/events | get the log for a case |

---

## Background jobs

Rails spec used ActiveJob names as placeholders, FastAPI equivalent to be decided in phase 5 (BackgroundTasks vs Celery).

- **ClassifyCaseJob** — calls the AI classification service asynchronously so the create-case request doesn't block on it
- **AutoResolveJob** — auto-resolves cases meeting certain low-severity, no-activity criteria
- **EscalationCheckJob** — periodic check for cases that should be escalated based on time-in-state or severity
---

## Service layer

Rails spec used service objects, FastAPI equivalent is a `services/` module with plain Python classes or functions doing the same job.

- **AiClassifier** — wraps the Claude API call, handles the request/response and failure cases
- **CaseRouter** — assigns a queue based on severity and category
- **CaseResolver** — handles the logic of closing a case
- **CaseEscalator** — handles moving a case into escalated state and any side effects (notifications, queue reassignment)
